Package: gnome-wifi-hotspot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erhan Zeyrek <erhanzeyrek@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, network-manager, hostapd, dnsmasq-base, iw, iproute2, iptables, polkitd, dbus
Suggests: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Homepage: https://github.com/3togo/gnome-wifi-hotspot
Description: Wi-Fi Relay hotspot with concurrent Wi-Fi connection sharing
 Share a Wi-Fi connection through a virtual access point from GNOME Shell
 Quick Settings or a desktop tray on XFCE. Includes a GTK4 settings application,
 a system D-Bus daemon,
 and automatic fallback to a permitted 2.4 GHz upstream access point.
 Concurrent operation requires compatible wireless hardware and drivers.
